WG Manager certificate layout
=============================

The Debian packages do not ship private keys or certificates.

Authentication/frontend host
----------------------------

/etc/wg-manager/cert/ca.crt
    root:root, mode 0644

/etc/wg-manager/cert/auth/auth.crt
    root:wg-auth, mode 0644
/etc/wg-manager/cert/auth/auth.key
    root:wg-auth, mode 0640

/etc/wg-manager/cert/client/client.crt
    root:wg-client, mode 0644
/etc/wg-manager/cert/client/client.key
    root:wg-client, mode 0640

/etc/wg-manager/cert/apache/apache-client.pem
    root:www-data, mode 0640

Controller host
---------------

/etc/wg-manager/cert/ca.crt
    root:root, mode 0644

/etc/wg-manager/cert/controller/server.crt
    root:wg-manager, mode 0644
/etc/wg-manager/cert/controller/server.key
    root:wg-manager, mode 0640

The package postinst scripts correct ownership and mode for files that already
exist when the package is configured. Certificates copied later must be given
the same ownership and permissions before the services are enabled.

Services are deliberately not enabled or started automatically by the package.
After installing certificates and editing the production configuration, enable
the required units explicitly.
